cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this reference or its data, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Dere Types: An Open Reference to Dere Character Archetypes for Fiction and AI Character Design"
abstract: >-
  An open reference guide and machine-readable taxonomy of Japanese-inspired
  dere character archetypes (tsundere, yandere, kuudere, dandere, deredere,
  himedere, oujidere, kamidere, sadodere, mayadere, bakadere), with canonical
  definitions, behavioral patterns, relationship patterns, common
  misconceptions, and guidance for AI character design. Dere types are treated
  as fictional character archetypes and fandom terminology, not psychological
  categories.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Williams"
    given-names: "Garret E."
  - name: "ChatBrat"
    website: "https://chatbrat.ai/"
  - name: "Dere Types contributors"
